(123822, 5789, 875, '<td valign="top">Stunningly beautiful color.  Outside of DPC, I''d recommend cloning out the floating stuff at the upper left, but I''m not taking points off for it in the score.</td>', 'Stunningly beautiful color.  Outside of DPC, I''d recommend cloning out the floating stuff at the upper left, but I''m not taking points off for it in the score.', '2002-09-19 19:34:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(123823, 5789, 82, '<td valign="top">I absolutely love the vivid colors!  The framing is very nice, and I like how the blue gradates into black below.  (Was this taken through glass?  If so, you did a terrific job of eliminating glare.)  Id like to see a stronger use of the negative space, but Im not sure what to suggest.  Its been a difficult week for voting, mainly due to my wildly subjective interpretations of the challenge.  Attractive photo, though, in any case!  7</td>', 'I absolutely love the vivid colors!  The framing is very nice, and I like how the blue gradates into black below.  (Was this taken through glass?  If so, you did a terrific job of eliminating glare.)  Id like to see a stronger use of the negative space, but Im not sure what to suggest.  Its been a difficult week for voting, mainly due to my wildly subjective interpretations of the challenge.  Attractive photo, though, in any case!  7', '2002-09-20 13:49:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(123824, 5789, 3111, '<td valign="top">Great shot, when you are "allowed" to spot edit, I would take out the flecks (other jellyfish?) in the deep blue water.  I hope you put some good technical details in this, I want to know how you did it.  8 - MarkRob</td>', 'Great shot, when you are "allowed" to spot edit, I would take out the flecks (other jellyfish?) in the deep blue water.  I hope you put some good technical details in this, I want to know how you did it.  8 - MarkRob', '2002-09-21 01:08:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(123825, 5789, 3087, '<td valign="top">The colours in this are simply stunning - that cobalt blue against the orangey yellow with the white trails... This would be an 8 for me if the white and blue marks at the top left were cleaned, which I appreciate you can''t spot edit for DPC entries, but have no doubt already done for your own master copy? I also like the composition very much.<br/>7, Kavey</td>', 'The colours in this are simply stunning - that cobalt blue against the orangey yellow with the white trails... This would be an 8 for me if the white and blue marks at the top left were cleaned, which I appreciate you can''t spot edit for DPC entries, but have no doubt already done for your own master copy? I also like the composition very much.7, Kavey', '2002-09-21 13:26:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(123826, 5789, 2109, '<td valign="top">Nice shot ... the specs of  "stuff" visible in the upper left are a bit annoying, but too bad you couldn''t edit those out ;)   Good shot, and good use of negative space  -8</td>', 'Nice shot ... the specs of  "stuff" visible in the upper left are a bit annoying, but too bad you couldn''t edit those out ;)   Good shot, and good use of negative space  -8', '2002-09-21 18:03:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(123827, 5789, 1037, '<td valign="top">This is incredibly beautiful! I love the delicacy of the jellyfish and the vivid colours. The space gives the sense that these are drifting freely in the water. I''ve given out so many 10s this week, but this is stunning, so here goes another one - lisae</td>', 'This is incredibly beautiful! I love the delicacy of the jellyfish and the vivid colours. The space gives the sense that these are drifting freely in the water. I''ve given out so many 10s this week, but this is stunning, so here goes another one - lisae', '2002-09-22 11:36:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(123828, 5789, 3955, '<td valign="top">great shot!  I know you cannot do it on this site, but when you clean up some of the white flecks you will have an even more amazing photo</td>', 'great shot!  I know you cannot do it on this site, but when you clean up some of the white flecks you will have an even more amazing photo', '2002-09-22 12:46:00.000000', NULL, 1),
