(125348, 5882, 82, '<td valign="top">To me, this photo poses a friendly debate over which of the spaces is the negative space.  It''s the debate that keeps me interested, after the initial grin at this poor soul clinging to the edge.  I would have preferred a perfectly even white area (the line is a tiny bit crooked), but the general composition is right on.  Good lighting (maybe a bit more contrast?) and good use of negative space up top ... it weighs down on top of the fingers.  8</td>', 'To me, this photo poses a friendly debate over which of the spaces is the negative space.  It''s the debate that keeps me interested, after the initial grin at this poor soul clinging to the edge.  I would have preferred a perfectly even white area (the line is a tiny bit crooked), but the general composition is right on.  Good lighting (maybe a bit more contrast?) and good use of negative space up top ... it weighs down on top of the fingers.  8', '2002-09-20 07:57:00.000000', NULL, 1),
