(166106, 5770, 5023, '<td valign="top">my wife''s mother is from iceland.  we live in michigan, USA.  This is a great shot,  I cant say enough about it.  I''m speachless.  if i was a member at the time of this challenge i would have voted a big 10</td>', 'my wife''s mother is from iceland.  we live in michigan, USA.  This is a great shot,  I cant say enough about it.  I''m speachless.  if i was a member at the time of this challenge i would have voted a big 10', '2002-12-07 16:33:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(166136, 5770, 5023, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Jubei Kibagami:</b></div><hr/><i>Nice,  I tried to do a couple flame shots once.  I learned that keeping rubbing alcohol in my mouth while I''m trying to light the match and then get my little torch going is not the way to do it.  You should have cropped just a bit more above the flame to get everything in it.  I like how his arms and head are just lit up.  9</i></td></tr></table> <br/>I cant believe all the people that think all the shots are cropped in some way.  me and alot of other photographer dont ever crop anything.  the shot simply is, what it is.  I havent cropped a shot in about 10 years</td>', 'Originally posted by Jubei Kibagami:Nice,  I tried to do a couple flame shots once.  I learned that keeping rubbing alcohol in my mouth while I''m trying to light the match and then get my little torch going is not the way to do it.  You should have cropped just a bit more above the flame to get everything in it.  I like how his arms and head are just lit up.  9 I cant believe all the people that think all the shots are cropped in some way.  me and alot of other photographer dont ever crop anything.  the shot simply is, what it is.  I havent cropped a shot in about 10 years', '2002-12-07 18:13:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(166408, 5898, 2553, '<td valign="top">Yes, my husband did hold still like that for the whole 8 seconds ! He''s a great model.  It was also "set up".  In fact, I think in total, I took about 30 shots until I got the look that I was going for - I''d take 5 or 10 ten shots, dump them onto the computer to see how they looked, then go back and try again.  It was a lot of fun, but more important for me, it taught me a lot about shutter speed and aperture, and how to achieve an effect. <br/>Linda</td>', 'Yes, my husband did hold still like that for the whole 8 seconds ! He''s a great model.  It was also "set up".  In fact, I think in total, I took about 30 shots until I got the look that I was going for - I''d take 5 or 10 ten shots, dump them onto the computer to see how they looked, then go back and try again.  It was a lot of fun, but more important for me, it taught me a lot about shutter speed and aperture, and how to achieve an effect. Linda', '2002-12-08 10:45:31.000000', NULL, 0),
