(123256, 5760, 259, '<td valign="top">it seems as though no matter what the challenge is, there always seems to be a bird on a wire shot taken.  thanks for keeping the streak alive.  on a serious note, i really like the symetry of the line going from corner to corner.</td>', 'it seems as though no matter what the challenge is, there always seems to be a bird on a wire shot taken.  thanks for keeping the streak alive.  on a serious note, i really like the symetry of the line going from corner to corner.', '2002-09-18 21:43:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(123257, 5760, 3102, '<td valign="top">Nice &amp; sharp -- very good!  One thing I remember learning in college while we were being taught about composition... for whatever artsy fartsy reason, they say you''re not supposed to have elements originating out of the corners of shots.  In other words, to suit the real art critics, the power line shouldn''t come directly out of the corners, it should be off-set a bit.  Anyway, that''s just for what it''s worth :)</td>', 'Nice & sharp -- very good!  One thing I remember learning in college while we were being taught about composition... for whatever artsy fartsy reason, they say you''re not supposed to have elements originating out of the corners of shots.  In other words, to suit the real art critics, the power line shouldn''t come directly out of the corners, it should be off-set a bit.  Anyway, that''s just for what it''s worth :)', '2002-09-18 23:18:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(123258, 5760, 82, '<td valign="top">The parallel lines divide this photo wonderfully, and the placement of the bird is great!  Very nicely composed.  The negative space emphasizes the unobtainable character of the bird, because it is framed high in the upper left, and the background is all sky.  8</td>', 'The parallel lines divide this photo wonderfully, and the placement of the bird is great!  Very nicely composed.  The negative space emphasizes the unobtainable character of the bird, because it is framed high in the upper left, and the background is all sky.  8', '2002-09-20 08:06:00.000000', NULL, 1),
