(123385, 5764, 1005, '<td valign="top">Wonderful shot.  Can''t wait to see the details for this one.  I don''t have anything to suggest, it''s great.  I am not commenting on negative space, even though I think I understand it pretty well, I am obviously not understanding it well enough from the stand point of other artists.  Great shot!  10 Swash</td>', 'Wonderful shot.  Can''t wait to see the details for this one.  I don''t have anything to suggest, it''s great.  I am not commenting on negative space, even though I think I understand it pretty well, I am obviously not understanding it well enough from the stand point of other artists.  Great shot!  10 Swash', '2002-09-19 18:41:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(123386, 5764, 3416, '<td valign="top">Excellent image, good use of the negative space, congratulations to the model.</td>', 'Excellent image, good use of the negative space, congratulations to the model.', '2002-09-19 19:40:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(123387, 5764, 1827, '<td valign="top">Neat!  Okay, so I''m confused...?  How-to coming?  It certainly appears that the face (facing right) is the one below the water, given the bubbles in the eyelashes and near the nose.  So, did you take this shot from below water surface?  Anyway, neat shot which created neat neg space around the faces.  7, just-married</td>', 'Neat!  Okay, so I''m confused...?  How-to coming?  It certainly appears that the face (facing right) is the one below the water, given the bubbles in the eyelashes and near the nose.  So, did you take this shot from below water surface?  Anyway, neat shot which created neat neg space around the faces.  7, just-married', '2002-09-19 23:57:00.000000', NULL, 1),
