(123658, 5783, 82, '<td valign="top">There are many shots this week of a subject near the lower region of the image with oceans of background.  To me, many of these lack a creative or interesting use of that space.  In this photo, however, I see a whimsical punch line, cleverly done.  The open sky is a comic yarn leading the viewer to a resolution of three cows.  Mildly absurdist, it reminds me of the smartly mysterious philosophy in Douglas Adams So Long, and Thanks For All The Fish, with a smack of Gary Larson for good measure.  Great shot!  Im glad you waited for the last cow to look straight at the camera.  9</td>', 'There are many shots this week of a subject near the lower region of the image with oceans of background.  To me, many of these lack a creative or interesting use of that space.  In this photo, however, I see a whimsical punch line, cleverly done.  The open sky is a comic yarn leading the viewer to a resolution of three cows.  Mildly absurdist, it reminds me of the smartly mysterious philosophy in Douglas Adams So Long, and Thanks For All The Fish, with a smack of Gary Larson for good measure.  Great shot!  Im glad you waited for the last cow to look straight at the camera.  9', '2002-09-19 10:24:00.000000', NULL, 1),
