(124246, 5819, 2764, '<td valign="top">According to my art school definition, this is one of the best uses of negative space.  If you remove the subject, the other spaces are still interesting,  Nice composition and colors all green.  I wonder if the point that is in perfect focus is right- is that the focal point of the picture?  I would have rather had the stub of the stem in focus or else the top leaf, instead of the iddle of the leaf stems.  How about 9?</td>', 'According to my art school definition, this is one of the best uses of negative space.  If you remove the subject, the other spaces are still interesting,  Nice composition and colors all green.  I wonder if the point that is in perfect focus is right- is that the focal point of the picture?  I would have rather had the stub of the stem in focus or else the top leaf, instead of the iddle of the leaf stems.  How about 9?', '2002-09-17 10:29:00.000000', NULL, 1),
