(125126, 5872, 3080, '<td valign="top">Not quite sure what the subject is here, so I can''t really identify the neg. space.  For neg. space to work, by  definition, there needs to be a subject, and the space that is not used up by the subject is the neg. space.  I do see what you are trying to convey here...the room is empty, leaving space.  However, empty space in a room, and negetive space in a photo are not really the same thing.  I believe this challenge was aimed toward people who have art or photography background, and I will not hold it against you..so...challenge met.  That being said, I like the use of the reflection in the window.  The photo is a bit dark for my taste, however I do like the addition of the light to the left.  The angle and framing are good, and the focus and clarity also are good.  Overall, the photo it''s self is very nice. Good luck in the challenge. ~hbunch7187~</td>', 'Not quite sure what the subject is here, so I can''t really identify the neg. space.  For neg. space to work, by  definition, there needs to be a subject, and the space that is not used up by the subject is the neg. space.  I do see what you are trying to convey here...the room is empty, leaving space.  However, empty space in a room, and negetive space in a photo are not really the same thing.  I believe this challenge was aimed toward people who have art or photography background, and I will not hold it against you..so...challenge met.  That being said, I like the use of the reflection in the window.  The photo is a bit dark for my taste, however I do like the addition of the light to the left.  The angle and framing are good, and the focus and clarity also are good.  Overall, the photo it''s self is very nice. Good luck in the challenge. ~hbunch7187~', '2002-09-16 20:30:00.000000', NULL, 1),
