(125613, 5898, 527, '<td valign="top">Very well done. Perhaps a little more information or detail in the hands. This meets the theme quite well.<br/><br/>T</td>', 'Very well done. Perhaps a little more information or detail in the hands. This meets the theme quite well.T', '2002-09-22 20:39:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(125614, 5898, 1280, '<td valign="top">Even though I HATE smoking (we ex-smokers are the least tolerant) I love this image.  Very, very nice. Strikes me as a cowboy, and reminds me a little of my own beloved husband.  Good use of neg space to meet the challenge, but what I like best is the wonderful lighting and coloring.  Good luck in the challenge!  Grayce aka Gracious</td>', 'Even though I HATE smoking (we ex-smokers are the least tolerant) I love this image.  Very, very nice. Strikes me as a cowboy, and reminds me a little of my own beloved husband.  Good use of neg space to meet the challenge, but what I like best is the wonderful lighting and coloring.  Good luck in the challenge!  Grayce aka Gracious', '2002-09-22 20:44:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(125615, 5898, 2553, '<td valign="top">At a night race (AHDRA Motorcycle Racing) some years ago, my husband was walking away from me and stopped to light a cigarette.  All I could see in the dark was his face lit by the lighter and cigarette.  The whole "picture" looked very mysterious and intriguing and I loved how the "negative space" of the dark emphasized his face.  I have always planned to do a painting based on that image in my mind, but thought that it was perfect for the Neg Spc challenge. Thank you for all the great comments, I appreciate everyone''s time - and congrats to all, I loved the images in this challenge.<br/>Linda</td>', 'At a night race (AHDRA Motorcycle Racing) some years ago, my husband was walking away from me and stopped to light a cigarette.  All I could see in the dark was his face lit by the lighter and cigarette.  The whole "picture" looked very mysterious and intriguing and I loved how the "negative space" of the dark emphasized his face.  I have always planned to do a painting based on that image in my mind, but thought that it was perfect for the Neg Spc challenge. Thank you for all the great comments, I appreciate everyone''s time - and congrats to all, I loved the images in this challenge.Linda', '2002-09-23 17:54:00.000000', NULL, 0),
